WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:08.720
Itadori Yuji is a fantastic character, not because&nbsp;
he is the vessel for Sukuna, the King of Curses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:13.200
but because of how human he is.&nbsp;
Despite his superhuman strength,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.880
enhanced reflexes and innate ability to&nbsp;
contain one of the biggest threats to humanity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:24.560
he has one defining characteristic that is&nbsp;
often overlooked: His selfish selflessness.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:29.680
While in many ways Itadori Yuji appears&nbsp;
to be your typical Shounen protagonist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:35.040
there is a reason why the story surrounding him&nbsp;
has gotten as popular and enjoyable as it has.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.800
Itadori is one of the most relatable&nbsp;
characters I have ever come across.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:57.840
He’s charming, friendly, and easygoing.&nbsp;
But he is also one of the loneliest.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:06.080
On the surface, Itadori is your typical shounen&nbsp;
protagonist High School student. As many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:12.720
'straightforward' protagonists, he gets portrayed&nbsp;
as kind, adventurous and somewhat “simple”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:17.520
academically speaking. However in his case, this&nbsp;
is a little bit less extreme as with some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:22.800
more idealistic characters such as Luffy, Naruto&nbsp;
or Asta. While these characters represent certain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:28.480
ideals expressed on a grander scale that the&nbsp;
audience can look up to, I think Itadori embodies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:33.840
a much more down-to-earth and genuine version of&nbsp;
these traits, with his one and only goal being to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:43.440
live by the last words of his grandfather:&nbsp;
お前は強いから人を助けろ. (insert subtitles in video).

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:48.720
And that makes him less of an unattainable&nbsp;
ideal and more of a relatable equal.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.120
A big portion of Itadori's charm comes from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:56.640
him being overall just a regular guy who&nbsp;
seems pretty fun to spend an afternoon with.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:00.160
This also makes him a much more&nbsp;
flexible and malleable character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:04.960
with the ability to look past animosity&nbsp;
and make friends of enemies. We can see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:10.400
this in his relationship with Junpei, and&nbsp;
again with his instant besto friendo, Todo.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:19.200
However, Akutami doesn't shove it into our&nbsp;
face that Yuji is a nice person by having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:24.960
him deliver major speeches, or having other&nbsp;
characters talk about what a great guy he is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:31.520
Instead, he leaves it for us to decide what we&nbsp;
think of him. He's pretty likable and extroverted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:37.520
but not overly so, and at times there is a certain&nbsp;
awkwardness in his interactions with his peers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:43.440
His strong points are of course his superhuman&nbsp;
strength and aptitude for JuJutsu. But I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:50.240
his actual strength comes from his extreme&nbsp;
altruism and ability to act on behalf of others.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:55.760
And yet, as any good protagonist and despite&nbsp;
Itadori being an awesome guy all around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.760 --> 00:03:01.920
he still of course also has his weaknesses. One&nbsp;
thing that isn't quite obvious from the start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:07.840
is that Itadori actually has a strong&nbsp;
sense of emptiness and loneliness.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:11.520
Since we know little about his past,&nbsp;
it's actually quite hard to tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:17.840
why this is the case despite his very&nbsp;
charismatic and extroverted nature.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:28.720
There is an answer to this question however.&nbsp;
I believe the fundamental flaw in Itadori's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:36.640
personality is the same as his strength. His&nbsp;
altruism. Itadori Yuji, just like Luffy &amp; co,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:42.640
is an absolute genius when it comes to people.&nbsp;
He's extremely good at understanding them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:47.520
what they are about, what drives them&nbsp;
and how to handle them. But while he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:52.400
excellent at reading others, he is&nbsp;
terrible at understanding himself.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:59.120
When we first meet Itadori, he has no path, no&nbsp;
drive and no meaningful relationships in his life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:04.800
except for his grumpy grandpa. At school, even&nbsp;
though he's notorious for his physique, he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:10.480
doesn't have any friends. He calls the two members&nbsp;
of the occultist club his friends, but they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:15.520
literally know nothing about him - also Itadori&nbsp;
only entered the club, so he could leave school&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:32.800
early and visit his grandpa in the first place.
And so, when he loses his grandpa, the only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:38.720
person he was ever close to, he falls into&nbsp;
grief and a very deep sense of loneliness.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:44.320
With no friends and no purpose and&nbsp;
presented with the world of JuJutsu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:50.800
Itadori latches onto his Grandfather's dying&nbsp;
wish, help others and die surrounded by friends.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:56.800
He is fully aware that this is probably not the&nbsp;
right thing to do, as he calls it his own curse.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:10.160
But with nothing else to hold&nbsp;
onto, it thus becomes his drive.&nbsp;

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:14.240
As a result, we see Itadori risking&nbsp;
his life on a regular bases,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:20.400
sometimes quite unnecessarily. More than once&nbsp;
he rushes into situations with no regard for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:25.680
his own health or life. And even though he&nbsp;
admits that he is scared of death, he seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:31.360
way too eager to sacrifice himself for others&nbsp;
and thus give his life meaning and purpose.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:37.520
This toxic mindset can be summarized like&nbsp;
this: 'I have to save and help others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:42.320
but I can't receive help from&nbsp;
anyone else. I must do it myself.'

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:46.720
This mindset by the way is also shared&nbsp;
by Itadori's counterpart Geto. And so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:53.280
while Itadori's altruism is very much real,&nbsp;
it is so extreme, that ironically enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:57.120
it starts to become selfish.&nbsp;
He wants to do anything and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:01.760
everything for others, so that in return he&nbsp;
gets validation and the permission to live.

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:05.920
The problem is, when you build&nbsp;
relationships based on this premise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:12.720
they inevitably fall apart sooner or later.&nbsp;
Relationships are built on mutual respect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:16.880
trust, and sacrifice. The&nbsp;
buzzword here being mutual.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:22.480
In fulfilling his grandfather’s wish and his&nbsp;
ultimate goal, Itadori Yuji acts on his own.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:27.520
I think that in searching for his purpose and&nbsp;
wanting to be needed, Yuji enters the lives of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:33.760
other people, probably unconsciously assuming&nbsp;
he can save them. He does so for Fushiguro and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:39.680
Junpei, but very much disliked it himself when&nbsp;
Todo does the very same thing to him at first.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:51.520
In short: Itadori looks for purpose and validation&nbsp;
by making everything in his life about others.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:57.840
Therefore, his character arc is all about learning&nbsp;
to form REAL relationships, built on mutual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:04.480
feeling, mutual hardship, mutual forgiveness and&nbsp;
mutual sacrifice. I think Itadori’s character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:10.640
needs to find a real purpose - not to die for&nbsp;
others, but one that’s worth staying alive for:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:16.160
forming bonds that give meaning to his life and&nbsp;
make him appreciate how precious it really is.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:20.400
The central theme and moral argument&nbsp;
of JuJutsu Kaisen is the question,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:25.760
what constitutes a good life that is worth&nbsp;
living. And Itadori, as the main protagonist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:30.320
is starting his arc with a very dangerous&nbsp;
and self-destructive answer to this question.

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:47.600
And yet, the skill with which Akutami is able to&nbsp;
expertly portray this weakness as an underlying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:54.560
part of Itadori's personality and only revealing&nbsp;
it in tiny bits shows his skills as a writer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:59.040
and makes Itadori immediately&nbsp;
relatable as a character.

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:05.360
Itadori Yuji is an extremely human and&nbsp;
realistic take on the common Shounen tropes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:10.160
that come very close to Togashi's way of&nbsp;
writing. However, I personally think that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:15.120
Itadori's arc will most likely come closer&nbsp;
to that of Killua from Darkness into light&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:21.520
rather than Gon's fall into darkness. And I would&nbsp;
even go so far as to say that Akutami's characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:27.600
are even a tad more complex and realistic in their&nbsp;
design – Satoru Gojo, Itadori’s mentor, comes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:39.840
mind here as well, who is eccentric, intimidating,&nbsp;
funny and so much more at the same time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:47.520
The deep personalities, complex motivations&nbsp;
and relationships all combined with the gory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:54.000
and fantasy element set in the real world have&nbsp;
created a fantastic story world for us to explore.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:09:04.400
And speaking of Gojo, you can watch his analysis&nbsp;
right here. Thanks so much for watching. Peace.

